+touch zero
+cat <<EOI >=1kb
A gzip file is a series of members, each of which holds the deflate data of
some original data between a header and a trailer. The header starts with
two identification bytes and the compression method, followed by the flags
that say which of the optional fields are present, the modification time of
the original data, the extra flags of the compression method, and the
operating system on which the compression took place. The optional fields
are an extra field of subfields, the original file name, a file comment, and
a CRC16 of the header itself. The trailer holds the CRC-32 of the original
data and its size modulo 2^32, which the decompressor verifies once it has
reached the end of the deflate data. The members of a file simply follow one
another, with nothing before, between, or after them, and the data of the
file is the data of all of its members, one after another. A decompressor
must check the identification bytes and the compression method, skip the
optional fields, and reject a member whose reserved flag bits are set, since
they may announce a field it doesn't know how to skip over.
EOI
+cat 1kb 1kb 1kb 1kb 1kb 1kb 1kb 1kb >=8kb
+cat 8kb 8kb 8kb 8kb 8kb 8kb 8kb 8kb >=64kb
+$* -c 6 --name a.txt <:'hello' >=hello
+$* -c 6 --name b.txt <:'world' >=world
+$* -c 6 <:'' >=void
+cat hello world >=hello-world

w = $~

: round-trip
: Compress into a stream and decompress from a stream
:
{{
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/zero | $* -d >>>$w/zero : zero
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/1kb  | $* -d >>>$w/1kb  : 1kb
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 64kb
  $* -c 0 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : store
  $* -c 9 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : smallest
}}

: members
: Decompress the data of several members
:
$* -d <<<$w/hello-world >:'helloworld'

: names
: Associate each character with the header of its member
:
{{
  : two
  :
  $* -d --names <<<$w/hello-world >:'[a.txt]hello[b.txt]world'

  : empty
  : Empty member, which no character comes from, between two others
  :
  cat $w/hello $w/void $w/world | $* -d --names >:'[a.txt]hello[b.txt]world'
}}

: limit
: File name longer than the limit
:
$* -d --limit 4 <<<$w/hello 2>>EOE != 0
error: file name longer than 4 bytes
EOE

: junk
: Data followed by something other than a member
:
cat $w/hello - <:'junk' | $* -d 2>>EOE != 0
error: expected identification byte 0x1f instead of 0x6a
EOE

: empty
: Stream without data
:
$* -d <<<$w/zero 2>>EOE != 0
error: empty gzip data
EOE
